imply focus on the  joy of driving it the V means lightning  bolt and refers to the cars driving  performance the little car from Japan  doesn't have to hide its light under a  stone it weighs 850 kilograms and goes  from 0 to 100 kilometers an hour in 9  seconds the chassis technology is solid  rigid axle suspended with leaf springs  were standard in compact car  construction in the 1970s  the Corolla showpieces  under the hood to double barrel  carburetors insure that the dual  overhead cam straight four-cylinder 1.6  liter engine purrs with power modeled on  Alfa Romeos of the time motorcycle  manufacturer Yamaha supported Toyota and  developing the cylinder head the growl  lets everyone know the Corolla isn't  just cute  Florian became a Toyota fan early on his  grandfather founded one of the first  Toyota outlets in Germany in 1975  Florian's dad and uncle Friedhelm later  took over the company in the 1980s in  addition to selling maintaining and  repairing current Toyota models Toyota  specialist Friedhelm Engel has got a  side job he restores classic cars  most of them vintage Toyotas this green  Celica is about finished it's being  completely rebuilt for his own  collection  if Florian has a problem or can't get  apart uncle fleet home always has a  solution  the area around home has plenty of  sinuous roads making it perfect driving  territory for Florian angle in his  levine he loves going out for rides in  his rare vehicle  and there's one thing the Toyota fan can  be certain of it's not likely he'll run  into someone with a car like his anytime  soon  in the next edition of driving a compact  SUV with the edges rounded off the new  Lexus NX 200t and a blast from the past  we take a 1974 VW Golf GTI out for a  spin
 

